  "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - Stream parser;\n  - ARM64 architecture;\n  - S390 architecture;\n  - x86 architecture;\n  - Compressed RAM block device driver;\n  - Bluetooth drivers;\n  - GPIO subsystem;\n  - GPU drivers;\n  - HID subsystem;\n  - Microsoft Hyper-V drivers;\n  - Hardware monitoring drivers;\n  - I2C subsystem;\n  - I3C subsystem;\n  - IIO subsystem;\n  - IIO ADC drivers;\n  - InfiniBand drivers;\n  - Input Device (Mouse) drivers;\n  - Input Device core drivers;\n  - Multiple devices driver;\n  - Media drivers;\n  - MemoryStick subsystem;\n  - MMC subsystem;\n  - MTD block device drivers;\n  - Network drivers;\n  - Ethernet team driver;\n  - NVME drivers;\n  - Device tree and open firmware driver;\n  - Operating Performance Points (OPP) driver;\n  - Power supply drivers;\n  - Voltage and Current Regulator drivers;\n  - Real Time Clock drivers;\n  - S/390 drivers;\n  - SCSI subsystem;\n  - Greybus lights staging drivers;\n  - Realtek RTL8723BS SDIO drivers;\n  - TCM subsystem;\n  - Trusted Execution Environment drivers;\n  - Thunderbolt and USB4 drivers;\n  - TTY drivers;\n  - Cadence USB3 driver;\n  - USB Device Class drivers;\n  - USB core drivers;\n  - DesignWare USB2 driver;\n  - USB Gadget drivers;\n  - USB Host Controller drivers;\n  - USB Serial drivers;\n  - USB Mass Storage drivers;\n  - USB Type-C Port Controller Manager driver;\n  - TI TPS6598x USB Power Delivery controller driver;\n  - Amazon Nitro Enclaves driver;\n  - Watchdog drivers;\n  - File systems infrastructure;\n  - BTRFS file system;\n  - Ceph distributed file system;\n  - F2FS file system;\n  - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;\n  - File system notification infrastructure;\n  - OCFS2 file system;\n  - SMB network file system;\n  - XFS file system;\n  - Tracing infrastructure;\n  - Kernel futex primitives;\n  - VLANs driver;\n  - KProbes tracing;\n  - Memory management;\n  - VMware vSockets driver;\n  - Netfilter;\n  - TCP network protocol;\n  - Audit subsystem;\n  - BPF subsystem;\n  - Perf events;\n  - Kernel command line parsing driver;\n  - Timer subsystem;\n  - Watch queue notification mechanism;\n  - Workqueue subsystem;\n  - Bluetooth subsystem;\n  - Ethernet bridge;\n  - Networking core;\n  - HSR network protocol;\n  - IPv4 networking;\n  - IPv6 networking;\n  - IUCV driver;\n  - MAC80211 subsystem;\n  - Management Component Transport Protocol (MCTP);\n  - Netlink;\n  - Open vSwitch;\n  - Packet sockets;\n  - RDS protocol;\n  - Network traffic control;\n  - SCTP protocol;\n  - SMC sockets;\n  - Sun RPC protocol;\n  - TIPC protocol;\n  - TLS protocol;\n  - Wireless networking;\n  - AppArmor security module;\n  - Key management;\n  - SELinux security module;\n  - ALSA framework;\n  - Analog Devices audio codecs;\n  - QCOM ASoC drivers;\n  - Samsung ASoC drivers;\n  - USB sound devices;\n  - Virtio sound driver;\n(CVE-2022-49622, CVE-2022-50167, CVE-2023-52561, CVE-2023-53651,\nCVE-2023-53733, CVE-2024-49901, CVE-2025-38728, CVE-2025-40135,\nCVE-2026-31678, CVE-2026-46265, CVE-2026-53353, CVE-2026-64015,\nCVE-2026-64190, CVE-2026-74341, CVE-2026-74405, CVE-2026-74406,\nCVE-2026-74672, CVE-2026-74739, CVE-2026-80572, CVE-2026-80851,\nCVE-2026-80852, CVE-2026-80861, CVE-2026-80947, CVE-2026-89441,\nCVE-2026-89465, CVE-2026-89481, CVE-2026-89492, CVE-2026-89539,\nCVE-2026-89552, CVE-2026-89553, CVE-2026-89625, CVE-2026-89633,\nCVE-2026-89638, CVE-2026-89640, CVE-2026-89652, CVE-2026-89672,\nCVE-2026-89680, CVE-2026-89685, CVE-2026-89707, CVE-2026-89719,\nCVE-2026-89738, CVE-2026-89740, CVE-2026-89761, CVE-2026-89763,\nCVE-2026-89837, CVE-2026-89838, CVE-2026-89848, CVE-2026-89859,\nCVE-2026-89860, CVE-2026-89877, CVE-2026-89912, CVE-2026-89921,\nCVE-2026-89972, CVE-2026-89987, CVE-2026-89988, CVE-2026-90002,\nCVE-2026-90016, CVE-2026-90023, CVE-2026-90029, CVE-